# Grid Visualizer — a 35x50 Skia Atlas of dots; a number (initially 99) is turned into a text path and the dots inside it spring up/scale in staggered waves; each tap clears the grid (text=null) and 700 ms later shows a new random number.
# What this test covers: the initial "99", a tap with the full clear→new-number cycle settled, a tap during the
# 700 ms clear gap and one mid-wave (springs retargeted from mid-flight), a rapid burst whose overlapping
# timeouts race each other, taps at the canvas corners, a tap outside the canvas (ignored), a long press and a
# drag on the grid (tap fails, nothing changes), and a final settle.
context platform=ios
open "demos://animations/grid-visualizer"
wait "label=\"Close\"" 40000
wait 2500
# Full cycle.
press 201 440
wait 3000
# Tap again inside the 700 ms clear gap.
press 201 440
wait 300
press 201 440
wait 3000
# Tap in the middle of the springing wave.
press 201 440
wait 1100
press 201 440
wait 3000
# Rapid burst: overlapping clears and timeouts.
press 201 440 --count 6 --interval-ms 100
wait 3500
# Corners of the canvas.
press 60 285
wait 1500
press 340 600
wait 3000
# Outside the canvas: no gesture.
press 201 720
wait 1000
# Long press and a drag: the tap fails/still fires on touches up; nothing should break.
longpress 201 440 1200
wait 2500
gesture pan 120 400 150 80 500
wait 3000
wait "label=\"Close\"" 10000
press "label=\"Close\""
wait 1500
